Now the core SwitchingOrderService. Careful design:

- All do* methods are called inside IdempotencyService's TransactionTemplate — so they run in a transaction. Mark them @Transactional so if called directly (telemetry service uses some helpers?) they still have tx. REQUIRES_NEW recordHit suspends — fine.

TicketRow internal record. Let me write it.

```java
package com.example.starter.ticket;

@Service
public class SwitchingOrderService {
    public static final Duration VALIDITY = Duration.ofHours(24);
    private final JdbcTemplate jdbc;
    private final Clock clock;
    private final InterlockService interlockService;

    // row records
    record TicketRow(long id, String requestId, String intervalId, String title, String status,
                     String reviewerId, Instant issuedAt, Instant expiresAt, Instant createdAt, Instant updatedAt) {}
    record StepRow(long id, int seq, String operationType, String deviceId, String expectedState,
                   String status, String operatorId, String guardianId, Instant executedAt, boolean verified) {}
```

Methods:

create(CreateTicketRequest req): 
```java
Instant now = Instant.now(clock);
KeyHolder kh = new GeneratedKeyHolder();
jdbc.update(con -> { PreparedStatement ps = con.prepareStatement("INSERT INTO switching_ticket (request_id, interval_id, title, status, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (?,?,?,?,?,?)", Statement.RETURN_GENERATED_KEYS); ... }, kh);
long id = kh.getKey().longValue();
int seq = 1;
for (StepSpec s : req.steps()) insert step PENDING;
return detail(id);
```

H2 generated keys with GeneratedKeyHolder works.

review(id, req): ticket=mustLoad(id); if (!"DRAFT".equals(status)) throw conflict TICKET_STATE; update REVIEWED, reviewer_id, updated_at. return detail.

issue(id, req): ticket=mustLoad; if (!"REVIEWED") → 409 TICKET_STATE. try insert lock catch DuplicateKeyException → 409 CONCURRENT_TICKET. update status ISSUED, issued_at=now, expires_at=now+24h. return detail.

confirm(id, seq, req):
```java
TicketRow t = mustLoad(id);
refreshExpiry(t, true); // throws and marks EXPIRED
if (!ISSUED && !EXECUTING) throw 409 TICKET_STATE
if (operatorId.equals(guardianId)) throw 400 DOUBLE_CONFIRM_REQUIRED  (both @NotBlank already)
StepRow step = findStep(id, seq) or 404 STEP_NOT_FOUND
if (!PENDING) throw 409 STEP_STATE
Integer next = min seq pending; if (next == null || next != seq) throw 409 STEP_ORDER
InterlockResult r = interlockService.evaluate(step.operationType, step.deviceId);
if (r.blocked()) { interlockService.recordHit(id, seq, r.ruleCode(), r.detail()); throw conflict("INTERLOCK_BLOCKED", r.detail() + " [" + r.ruleCode() + "]"); }
update step DONE..., update device_state, update ticket EXECUTING if ISSUED + updated_at
return new ConfirmView(id, seq, "DONE", "EXECUTING");
```

Wait — recordHit is REQUIRES_NEW, then we throw → outer tx rolls back. The REQUIRES_NEW commits separately. Good. But REQUIRES_NEW on H2 with Hikari pool size 5 — needs a second connection; pool has 5, fine.

Hmm, but there's a deadlock risk: REQUIRES_NEW suspends outer tx which may hold locks (we've only done SELECTs, no locks in H2 by default for selects). Fine.

archive(id, req):
```java
TicketRow t = mustLoad(id);
if (ARCHIVED) return detail(id); // 幂等成功
t = refreshExpiry(t, false); // silent transition to EXPIRED
switch status: ISSUED, EXECUTING, EXCEPTION, EXPIRED → set ARCHIVED, delete lock; else 409 TICKET_STATE
return detail(id);
```

refreshExpiry(TicketRow t, boolean throwOnExpire):
```java
if ((ISSUED or EXECUTING) && t.expiresAt != null && !Instant.now(clock).isBefore(t.expiresAt)) {
    jdbc.update("UPDATE switching_ticket SET status='EXPIRED', updated_at=? WHERE id=?", now, id);
    releaseLock(t.intervalId, t.id);
    if (throwOnExpire) throw conflict("TICKET_EXPIRED", "操作票已满24小时作废");
    return mustLoad(id);
}
return t;
```

releaseLock: DELETE FROM interval_execution_lock WHERE interval_id=? AND ticket_id=?

get(id): detail.

detail(id): load ticket, steps, hits → TicketDetailView.

mustLoad: query, orElseThrow 404 TICKET_NOT_FOUND.

Also helper for telemetry service: 
- findActiveLockTicketId(intervalId) → Long
- handleTelemetryForTicket — I'll put telemetry logic in TelemetryService but it needs ticket internals: load ticket, find last unverified done step, mark verified, set EXCEPTION + release lock. To avoid duplicating, expose from SwitchingOrderService:
  - `Long activeTicketForInterval(String intervalId)` 
  - `String processTelemetry(long ticketId, String deviceId, String state)` returns "VERIFIED"/"ABORTED"/"RECORDED"
  - `boolean hasArchivedTicket(String intervalId)`
  - `void refreshExpirySilently(long ticketId)` 

Hmm, telemetry processing must be in same tx as telemetry insert. TelemetryService.record will be @Transactional and call SwitchingOrderService methods (@Transactional REQUIRED joins). OK.

processTelemetry(ticketId, deviceId, state):
```java
TicketRow t = mustLoad(ticketId);
t = refreshExpiry(t, false);
if (!ISSUED && !EXECUTING) return "RECORDED";
StepRow step = lastDoneUnverified(ticketId); // may be null
if (step != null && step.deviceId.equals(deviceId)) {
    if (step.expectedState.equals(state)) { mark verified; return "VERIFIED"; }
    else { update ticket EXCEPTION; releaseLock; return "ABORTED"; }
}
return "RECORDED";
